    "narrative": "Today\u2019s optimal lineup for Ghost Ride the WHIP leans heavily into favorable matchups against soft pitching rotations. **James Wood** (78.42) and **Mickey Moniak** (75.75) anchor our production, as both benefit from highly exploitable SP_xERA matchups against Young (4.76) and Paredes (5.42). **James Wood** is particularly well-positioned, as his elite xwOBA of .396 pairs perfectly with an aggressive park factor and top-of-the-order usage to provide our highest efficiency ceiling. Similarly, **Mickey Moniak** sees a massive +19% boost from the opposing SP skill, making him an essential start. **Josh Naylor** (67.55) and **Jose Caballero** (62.42) round out our tier-one plays; **Jose Caballero** remains a high-priority roster piece due to his sprint speed and the +2% bonus for a slow SP delivery, which significantly enhances his stolen base probability despite the presence of a left-handed starter.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Cole Young**, who fell just short of the cut at 46.67. While his speed metrics are intriguing, the combination of an elite opposing catcher and a lower-order slot (8) ultimately tipped the scales toward **Kyle Karros** (52.85), who benefits more from the porous Paredes matchup. We are closely monitoring lineup uncertainty for **Henry Bolte** and **Max Muncy** against the tough Reid Detmers; while **Henry Bolte** is locked into the starting outfield pending final confirmation, the volatility associated with his -16% SP skill adjustment makes his floor notably thin. Owners should also note that **Austin Riley** carries a warning due to a poor BvP history against Webb, though the wind blowing out offers just enough of a cushion to keep him in the starting mix.",
